    Software on the organization's behalf for its internal operations.
    The organization may earn revenue from its business activities while
    using the Covered Software internally. It may not sell the Covered
    Software or provide it as a product or hosted service to customers.

For clarity, an office may use Kerykeion Terminal for internal chat and
file transfers without paying a license fee, even if that office belongs
to a for-profit business.

